  - human in the loop
abstract: >-
  Red-team work on a production multi-agent fleet, written down. A threat model naming eight
  assets, six trust boundaries and ten untrusted input surfaces, with nine residual risks
  carrying numbers. A mapping of the running system onto the OWASP Top 10 for LLM
  Applications (2025) and MITRE ATLAS with exact identifiers, published together with the
  rows where the system is uncovered: fifteen ATLAS techniques reproduced on the authors own
  stand, ten more listed as applicable and untested, twelve ATLAS mitigations implemented and
  eight explicitly not. A measurement of the systems own authorization classifier reporting
  refusal and over-refusal as two separate rates plus a rule-coverage rate, which shows that
  fourteen of forty-nine must-ask actions reach a human only because the default is
  fail-closed. A six-way mutation suite, shown failing on broken code before it was shown
  passing. And a public write-up of an indirect prompt-injection chain delivered through four
  input surfaces to four agents, with the damage it caused measured side by side against the
  same fleet behind one authorization boundary.
